  "problem": "Suppose that $C$ and $D$ are sets. If $|C|=1$ and $|D|=6,$ then $|P(C)|+|P(D)|=$",
  "worked_solution": "For any set $S$, $|P(S)|={2}^{|S|}.$ \n\nIn this case, $|C|=1$ and $|D|=6,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(C)|+|P(D)| & ={2}^{|C|}+{2}^{|D|} \\\\  & ={2}^{1}+{2}^{6} \\\\  & =2+64 \\\\  & =66.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
